---
import BaseLayout from '../layouts/BaseLayout.astro';
import Breadcrumbs from '../components/Breadcrumbs.astro';
import { GATE } from '../lib/quality-gate';
import { breadcrumbList } from '../lib/schema';

// Bump the version and add a change note whenever the method changes.
const METHOD = { version: '0.1' };
const site = Astro.site ?? new URL(Astro.url.origin);
const crumbs = [
  { name: 'Home', path: '/' },
  { name: 'How we rank', path: '/methodology' },
];
const g = GATE.category;
const weights = [
  {
    part: 'Satisfaction',
    weight: '40%',
    detail:
      'Average overall rating, pulled toward the category average until a product has enough reviews, with recent reviews counting more than old ones.',
  },
  {
    part: 'Review confidence',
    weight: '20%',
    detail: 'Number of reviews, how each reviewer was verified, and the share of reviews the vendor did not request.',
  },
  {
    part: 'Value and price clarity',
    weight: '15%',
    detail: 'Value-for-money ratings, whether prices are published, and any costs outside the plan price.',
  },
  { part: 'Vendor responsiveness', weight: '10%', detail: 'Share of reviews the vendor answered, and support ratings.' },
  { part: 'Momentum', weight: '15%', detail: 'Change in rating and in verified review count over the last six months.' },
];
---

<BaseLayout
  title="How We Check Software Prices"
  description="Where each price comes from, how often we re-check it, and what the page says when a price is out of date. Plus the rules for listing a product."
  path="/methodology"
  jsonLd={[breadcrumbList(crumbs, site)]}
>
  <div class="mx-auto max-w-3xl px-4 py-8">
    <Breadcrumbs crumbs={crumbs} />
    <h1 class="mt-4 text-3xl font-bold tracking-tight">How we rank and list software</h1>
    <p class="mt-2 text-sm text-slate-500">Method version {METHOD.version}</p>

    <div class="editorial mt-8">
      <h2 id="inclusion">How a product gets listed</h2>
      <p>
        Each category has a short list of capabilities a product must have, written before any product is added. A
        product appears in the category only after we check each capability against the vendor's own documentation and
        record the page we used. No vendor can pay to be listed or to skip a requirement. A way for vendors to send us
        corrections is not set up yet.
      </p>

      <h2 id="gate">When a category opens</h2>
      <p>
        A category page stays out of search results until it holds enough checked data to help someone choose. The
        current thresholds are listed here, and the page stays visible to visitors in the meantime.
      </p>
      <ul>
        <li>
          At least {g.minQualifyingProducts} products that meet the inclusion criteria, or {GATE.subcategory.minQualifyingProducts}
          for a more specific subcategory
        </li>
        <li>
          At least {g.minCompleteProfiles} of those products with prices checked in the last
          {' '}{GATE.completeProfilePricingDays} days{GATE.launch.requireScreenshots ? ', and screenshots' : ''}
        </li>
        {
          GATE.launch.requireReviewsOrNotes ? (
            <li>
              At least {g.minReviews} verified reviews across the category, or our own hands-on notes on {g.minHandsOnProducts} products
            </li>
          ) : (
            <li>
              Reviews and screenshots are not required yet, because review collection has not opened. They will become a
              requirement once they exist, and this list will change when they do.
            </li>
          )
        }
        <li>At least {g.minEditorialWords} words of editorial copy, with the inclusion criteria approved and the copy signed off by the site's editor</li>
        <li>Editorial copy that shares less than {g.maxSimilarity * 100}% of its phrasing with any other page on the site</li>
      </ul>

      <h2 id="product-pages">When a product page opens</h2>
      <p>
        {
          GATE.launch.requireProductReviewsOrNote
            ? `A product page stays out of search results until it has at least ${GATE.product.minReviews} verified reviews or one of our own hands-on notes, a summary we wrote, and prices checked in the last ${GATE.stalePricingDays} days.`
            : `A product page is open to search engines when it is published, has a summary we wrote, has prices checked in the last ${GATE.stalePricingDays} days, and appears in at least one category page that is itself open. Reviews and hands-on notes are not required yet, because review collection has not opened. A page with a hands-on note will say so; we write one only after using the product ourselves.`
        }
      </p>

      <h2 id="scores">How scores will work</h2>
      <p>
        No product has a score yet, because review collection has not opened. When scores arrive, each one will combine
        the five parts below and link back to this table. The weights are a draft. We will settle them before the first
        score is published and note them here.
      </p>
    </div>

    <div class="mt-2 overflow-x-auto rounded-xl border border-slate-200 bg-white">
      <table class="data-table min-w-[32rem]">
        <caption class="sr-only">Draft score weights</caption>
        <thead>
          <tr><th scope="col">Part</th><th scope="col">Draft weight</th><th scope="col">What it measures</th></tr>
        </thead>
        <tbody>
          {
            weights.map((w) => (
              <tr>
                <th scope="row">{w.part}</th>
                <td>{w.weight}</td>
                <td class="text-slate-600">{w.detail}</td>
              </tr>
            ))
          }
        </tbody>
      </table>
    </div>

    <div class="editorial mt-6">
      <p>
        Company size and advertising spend are not inputs. A small product with recent, verified reviews can rank above
        a large one.
      </p>

      <h2 id="prices">How prices are checked</h2>
      <p>
        Each price comes from the vendor's public pricing page or a written quote, and the page links to it. We plan to
        check every price again within 90 days. When a price has gone {GATE.stalePricingDays} days without a new check, the page says so next to the price.
      </p>
      <p>
        Costs outside the plan price are listed separately. Common examples are single sign-on offered only on the top
        plan, setup fees, minimum seat counts and annual-only billing.
      </p>
      <p>
        Some vendors publish no price at all and only offer a quote or a demo. We still list them when their own pages
        confirm the features a category requires. The page says the vendor only quotes, and we record nothing we could
        not read on the vendor's site. The absence of a published price is noted on the page and counted in the value and
        price clarity part of the score.
      </p>

      <h2 id="reviews">How reviews will be verified</h2>
      <p>
        Review collection has not opened, so this describes the rules we will follow when it does. Every reviewer will
        confirm their identity with a work email address or a LinkedIn account before a review is published. Each review
        will show how the reviewer was verified and whether the vendor invited them. When a reviewer received a gift or
        payment, the review will say so, and the reward will never depend on the rating given.
      </p>
      <p>
        Vendors will be able to reply to reviews and to flag a review with a reason. They will not be able to remove
        reviews, and every removal will be counted on the product page together with its reason.
      </p>
    </div>
  </div>
</BaseLayout>
